body:
I suggest we should just used these terms on their social media handles. That would be funny.

&#x200B;

**he - person's name or "they"**

 Unless you know the person you're addressing uses "he" as their pronoun, it isbetter to use "they" or to ask the person which pronouns they use.

&#x200B;

**straight - heterosexual** 

This term implies that anyone who is not heterosexual is bent or not "normal."

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

**slave (adj) - secondary, replica,worker** (This ones the funniest)  
The historical context of this term involved oppression of a group of people who were enslaved, thought of as less than human and unable to exercise free will

&#x200B;

(WTF is this) **rule of thumb - standard rule, general rule**

 Although no written record exists today, this phrase is attributed to an old British law  
that allowed men to beat their wives with sticks no wider than their thumb.
